  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Planning Application Architecture**\n\nI\'m deep in the planning stages for the application architecture. I\'m focusing on a structured approach, carefully considering visual design elements alongside pure logic modules. The aim is to create a robust system with thorough unit tests and a comprehensive verification plan *before* generating images or writing code. It\'s a structured approach with the goal of creating a comprehensive architecture.\n\n\n**Refining Aesthetic Design**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the aesthetic design phase. My focus is on crafting a refined, memorable editorial-festival / architectural nightlife website for the AIML Freshers\' Party 2026, titled \"Epoch \'26.\" I\'ve settled on a deep nocturnal obsidian canvas as the primary color. Warm-cool charcoal surfaces provide contrast, with a crisp Warm Marigold accent. I\'m carefully checking the frontend design rules, ensuring no neon or gradient.\n\n\n**Defining Type & Layout**\n\nI\'ve moved on to solidify typography and top bar layout rules.  I\'m specifying the fonts, with particular emphasis on how they render in dark mode, and setting their loading via `index.html`. My 3-zone top bar contract for mobile and desktop is taking shape with precise positioning of the wordmark, navigation links, and the primary call-to-action button, ensuring mobile responsivity. I\'m focusing on a clean, uncluttered user experience.\n\n\n**Structuring Section Content**\n\nI\'m now detailing the application\'s section architecture, with a cohesive five-section narrative flow in mind. I\'ve designed the hero section as a full-width asymmetric split with editorial kickers, headlines, subtitles, and a prominent CTA alongside atmospheric photography. Below that, there\'s a 4-column event essentials strip. The \"Highlights & Competitions\" section will be an asymmetric Bento Grid, and the remaining sections will follow a clear structure.\n\n\n**Detailing Evening Experiences**\n\nI\'m currently crafting the \"Highlights\" section, which will feature four marquee experiences. I\'m focusing on the layout using a non-symmetrical structure with generated imagery and clean metadata, including times, locations, and descriptions. Then, I\'ll be working on an interactive, filterable timeline for the evening schedule, complete with segmented filter buttons and functional buttons.\n\n\n**Implementing Interactive Features**\n\nI\'ve been working on interactive elements, specifically an \"Added to My Plan\" toggle that updates a \"My Itinerary\" counter in the schedule toolbar using `localStorage`. I\'m now developing the \"Interactive Showcase\" section, a clean architectural split into dress code guidelines and an interactive party hub. The hub features tabs for both song requests, and Mr./Ms. AIML Sign-up, complete with request functionality. I\'m focusing on user persistence across sessions.\n\n\n**Developing Entry & Sign-up**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the core conversion funnel. I\'m building a robust RSVP form with real-time validation for full name, roll number, college email, section, dining preference, and event interest. Validation errors will be instantly visible with text and an icon. Concurrently, I\'m crafting a \"Talent Audition\" section where freshers can register for specific audition categories, alongside name, roll number, and a short pitch.\n\n\n**Designing Ticket System**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in developing the event ticket system. I\'ve designed an architectural boarding pass-style ticket with a unique pass code and a scannable QR matrix, both derived deterministically from the attendee\'s details. I\'ve also incorporated a download button for a PNG version, rendered via HTML5 Canvas. The pass will be stored in `localStorage` for easy reloading.\n\n\n\n**Verifying Key User Journeys**\n\nI\'m now focused on end-to-end user journey verification in a real browser. I\'m starting with the RSVP flow. I will check for empty form submission and validate error messages. Then, I\'ll submit valid data (\"Ananya Sharma\", \"26AIML042\", \"ananya.sharma@aiml.edu\", Section B, Vegetarian) to ensure the live digital pass is generated and displays correctly. I\'ll test validation rules for name, roll number, and college email.\n\n\n**Testing User Interaction**\n\nI\'m now focused on rigorous testing of interactive features and user flows. I\'m verifying data persistence by reloading the page after issuing a pass and confirming it\'s restored. I\'ll check schedule filtering, itinerary bookmarking, song request upvotes and submissions, and talent nomination workflows. I\'ll ensure full viewport responsiveness on desktop (1440x900) and mobile (390x844).\n\n\n**Generating Visuals & Images**\n\nI\'m now generating images in a single parallel turn, as per design specifications. I\'m focusing on four high-impact editorial images. I\'ve specified detailed prompts for each visual asset, ensuring they adhere to the required aesthetic and aspect ratios, including a hero image of a university gala and a DJ afterparty scene. My goal is to produce evocative imagery for the frontend.\n\n\n"
