  planner_response {
    response: "Built **Epoch \'26**, the official freshers\' party website for the **Department of AI & Machine Learning (Batch of 2026\342\200\2232030)**.\n\n### Key Features\n- **Hero & Live Countdown**: Asymmetric editorial hero featuring gala photography, event essentials (date, hours, venue, dress code), and a live `tabular-nums` countdown to doors opening.\n- **Signature Lineup**: Asymmetric Bento showcase highlighting the Open-Air DJ Set & Afterparty, Mr. & Ms. AIML \'26 pageant, Acoustic Sets & Crew Showcases, and Courtyard Gala Dinner & Polaroid Wall.\n- **Interactive Evening Schedule**: Chronological timeline with category filters (`All Events`, `Stage`, `Social`, `Dining`, and `My Plan`) plus persistent personal itinerary bookmarking.\n- **Dress Code Lookbook & Venue FAQ**: *Nocturnal Monochrome* style guide with lookbook photography and an expandable logistics accordion (gate requirements, audition timings, hostel shuttles, dining lanes).\n- **Fresher Participation Hub**:\n  - **DJ Song Queue**: Upvote existing tracks (auto-sorted by vote count) or request new songs with duplicate detection and validation.\n  - **Mr. & Ms. AIML / Talent Sign-up**: Reserve an audition slot across pageant and stage categories with live roster updates.\n- **Digital Entry Pass & RSVP**: Validated student registration form (name, roll number, email, section, dining preference, participation track) that generates a persistent official pass with an assigned check-in gate, deterministic pass code, unique SVG QR matrix, and one-click **Download Pass (PNG)** export.\n\n### Verification Summary\n- **Unit Tests**: Verified all 7 deterministic unit tests covering countdown math, RSVP validation, pass/QR matrix generation, schedule filtering, DJ queue voting/deduplication, and talent sign-up validation.\n- **Build & Type Check**: Verified clean production build and TypeScript linting with zero errors.\n- **Browser & Responsive Testing**: Verified at desktop (`1440x900`) and mobile (`390x844`) viewports with zero console errors and zero horizontal overflow across all interactive journeys (schedule filtering/bookmarking, song voting/submission, talent audition sign-up, RSVP validation/pass issuance, reload persistence, and mobile navigation drawer).\n- **Fixes Applied After Visual Review**: Stacked the Fresher Participation Hub header above its tab switcher to prevent cramped multi-line wrapping, removed the trailing separator dot on narrow mobile screens in the hero department kicker, strengthened contrast scrims over the lineup cards, and added sticky-header scroll clearance (`scroll-mt-20`) to all anchor sections."
    message_id: "zbQBa4ziK9utz7IPgYDPkQI"
    modified_response: "Built **Epoch \'26**, the official freshers\' party website for the **Department of AI & Machine Learning (Batch of 2026\342\200\2232030)**.\n\n### Key Features\n- **Hero & Live Countdown**: Asymmetric editorial hero featuring gala photography, event essentials (date, hours, venue, dress code), and a live `tabular-nums` countdown to doors opening.\n- **Signature Lineup**: Asymmetric Bento showcase highlighting the Open-Air DJ Set & Afterparty, Mr. & Ms. AIML \'26 pageant, Acoustic Sets & Crew Showcases, and Courtyard Gala Dinner & Polaroid Wall.\n- **Interactive Evening Schedule**: Chronological timeline with category filters (`All Events`, `Stage`, `Social`, `Dining`, and `My Plan`) plus persistent personal itinerary bookmarking.\n- **Dress Code Lookbook & Venue FAQ**: *Nocturnal Monochrome* style guide with lookbook photography and an expandable logistics accordion (gate requirements, audition timings, hostel shuttles, dining lanes).\n- **Fresher Participation Hub**:\n  - **DJ Song Queue**: Upvote existing tracks (auto-sorted by vote count) or request new songs with duplicate detection and validation.\n  - **Mr. & Ms. AIML / Talent Sign-up**: Reserve an audition slot across pageant and stage categories with live roster updates.\n- **Digital Entry Pass & RSVP**: Validated student registration form (name, roll number, email, section, dining preference, participation track) that generates a persistent official pass with an assigned check-in gate, deterministic pass code, unique SVG QR matrix, and one-click **Download Pass (PNG)** export.\n\n### Verification Summary\n- **Unit Tests**: Verified all 7 deterministic unit tests covering countdown math, RSVP validation, pass/QR matrix generation, schedule filtering, DJ queue voting/deduplication, and talent sign-up validation.\n- **Build & Type Check**: Verified clean production build and TypeScript linting with zero errors.\n- **Browser & Responsive Testing**: Verified at desktop (`1440x900`) and mobile (`390x844`) viewports with zero console errors and zero horizontal overflow across all interactive journeys (schedule filtering/bookmarking, song voting/submission, talent audition sign-up, RSVP validation/pass issuance, reload persistence, and mobile navigation drawer).\n- **Fixes Applied After Visual Review**: Stacked the Fresher Participation Hub header above its tab switcher to prevent cramped multi-line wrapping, removed the trailing separator dot on narrow mobile screens in the hero department kicker, strengthened contrast scrims over the lineup cards, and added sticky-header scroll clearance (`scroll-mt-20`) to all anchor sections."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
